<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bilge Qaghan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 734</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Bilge</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bilge Qaghan was a ruler of the Second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Göktürk Khaganate</a> who consolidated the state in the early eighth century. Under him a single exchange with the Tang emperor Xuanzong produced 100,000 bolts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> for thirty horses, illustrating Göktürk extraction from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. He died in 734, reportedly poisoned by his own chancellor, and his death helped bring about the collapse of the Gokturk Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bilge-qaghan.jpg" alt="Bilge Qaghan" width="320" height="361" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gary Todd from Xinzheng, China · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Turkic_8th_Century_Marble_Statue_of_Bilge_Khan_(35580731981).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
